One way to allocate the points fairly is to use a random allocation method. Here's a Matlab code that implements this method:
```
% Set the number of players and total points
num_players = 4;
total_points = 10;
% Allocate points randomly to each player
points = randi([0, min(5, total_points)], [1, num_players]);
while sum(points) ~= total_points
    % If the total points allocated is not equal to the total points, adjust the allocation
    idx = find(points > 5, 1);
    if ~isempty(idx)
        % If a player has more than 5 points, reduce their allocation
        points(idx) = randi([0, min(5, total_points - sum(points) + points(idx))]);
    else
        % If no player has more than 5 points, increase a random player's allocation
        idx = randi(num_players);
        points(idx) = min(5, total_points - sum(points) + points(idx));
    end
end
% Display the allocation
disp(points);
